# ⚠️ DEPRECATED — per-environment files are now used instead.
#
#   .env.dev.example   → copy to .env.dev    (dev/staging Supabase project)
#   .env.prod.example  → copy to .env.prod   (production Supabase project)
#
# Why: every ops command now names its target explicitly, so a stale shell
# variable can't point a migration loop at production by accident:
#
#   SSMS_ENV=dev  ./scripts/db.sh migrate
#   SSMS_ENV=prod ./scripts/db.sh migrate     # prompts for confirmation
#
# See scripts/env.sh for the guardrails and supabase/README.md for the commands.
#
# A plain `.env` is still honoured as a fallback for local one-offs, but prefer
# .env.dev so the app and scripts read the same file.
#
# Mailer settings (all optional, see src/mailer/README.md): RESEND_API_KEY,
# MAIL_FROM, MAIL_REPLY_TO, EMAIL_LOGO_URL, PORTAL_URL.
#
# Supabase Send Email hook secret (v1,whsec_<base64>): SEND_EMAIL_HOOK_SECRET.
#
# Daily reminders (see .env.prod.example): REMINDERS_SCHEDULE_ENABLED (default
# true in production, false otherwise), REMINDERS_HOUR_TORONTO (default 11).
#
# Live storefront page base for instructor links (GET /me/go-live `liveUrl`):
# STOREFRONT_LIVE_BASE_URL (default https://ssnow.club/pages/our-team/).
